        "frame": {
            "$comment_adapter": "Not a screen. A Remote Compose widget is drawn into a host container of a fixed size, so the frame is the host, not a watch face: `frame/widget-host` rather than the sibling catalog's `frame/round-screen`. This is the second reason `remote-m3` is a catalog of its own rather than a mode of the Wear one.",
            "adapter": "frame/widget-host",
            "geometry": {
                "$comment": "The two host sizes are DECLARED BY THE PREVIEW CONTRACT, not measured after the fact: remote-catalog/src/main/kotlin/ee/schimke/wearm3catalog/remote/WidgetContainerPreviews.kt pins @Preview(widthDp = 216, heightDp = 76) and (216, 124), being 200x60dp and 200x108dp of content plus 8dp of padding on every edge. Every widget sticker in this catalog renders at one of them, so they are the sizes a builder must offer. Recorded here rather than transcribed into the server, which carried both numbers as constants.",
                "sizesDp": [
                    {
                        "widthDp": 216,
                        "heightDp": 76,
                        "label": "Small container"
                    },
                    {
                        "widthDp": 216,
                        "heightDp": 124,
                        "label": "Large container"
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        "code": null,
        "templates": [],
        "colorTokens": {
            "$comment": "The theme roles a colour property may name. Same Material 3 vocabulary as the sibling :catalog, and stated here for the same reason: a Remote design names roles, and a role the canvas cannot resolve is a literal. Every sticker in this catalog is a RemoteDocument carrying explicit dark-first Material colours, so the values behind these names are the document's rather than a theme's — but the names are what a design writes.",
            "roles": [
                "background",
                "surface",
                "surfaceContainer",
                "surfaceContainerLow",
                "surfaceContainerHigh",
                "surfaceContainerHighest",
                "primary",
                "onPrimary",
                "tertiary",
                "onTertiary",
                "onSurface",
                "onSurfaceVariant",
                "outlineVariant",
                "transparent"
            ]
        },
